=encoding utf8

=head1 NAME

std/io/socks - socket programming helpers for Zuzu.

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  from std/io/socks import *;

  let srv := listen_tcp( "127.0.0.1", 0 );
  let cli := connect_tcp( "127.0.0.1", srv.port() );
  let peer := srv.accept();

  cli.say( "hello" );
  let line := peer.next_line();

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This module provides a practical API for TCP, UDP, and Unix domain
sockets.

When possible, method names mirror other stream APIs:
C<read>, C<write>, C<print>, C<say>, C<next_line>,
C<each_line>, and C<close>.

=head1 FUNCTIONS

=over

=item C<< listen_tcp(String host?, Number port?, Number backlog?) >>

Create a TCP listening socket and return C<TCPServer>.

=item C<< connect_tcp(String host, Number port, Bool raw?) >>

Connect to a TCP server and return C<TCPSocket>.

=item C<< bind_udp(String host?, Number port?, Bool raw?) >>

Bind a UDP socket and return C<UDPSocket>.

=item C<< connect_udp(String host, Number port, Bool raw?) >>

Create a connected UDP socket and return C<UDPSocket>.

=item C<< listen_unix(String path, Number backlog?) >>

Create a Unix domain stream server and return C<UnixServer>.

=item C<< connect_unix(String path, Bool raw?) >>

Connect to a Unix domain stream server and return C<UnixSocket>.

=back

=head1 CLASSES

=head2 Socket methods

Common methods include C<read>, C<write>, C<print>, C<say>,
C<next_line>, C<each_line>, C<close>, and C<is_open>.

=head2 TCPSocket

Adds C<peer_host> and C<peer_port>.

=head2 TCPServer

Provides C<accept>, C<port>, C<host>, and C<close>.

=head2 UDPSocket

Provides C<send>, C<recv>, C<port>, C<host>, and C<close>.

=head2 UnixSocket / UnixServer

Unix sockets support stream methods, and C<UnixServer> offers
C<accept>, C<path>, and C<close>.

